[39.880227, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 10s left"]
[40.927055, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 9s left"]
[41.960692, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 8s left"]
[42.992042, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 7s left"]
[44.028937, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 6s left"]
[45.06722, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 4s left"]
[46.111743, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 3s left"]
[47.157677, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 2s left"]
[48.199244, "o", "\r\u001b[K   grace: 1s left"]
[49.240684, "o", "\r\n"]
[49.240774, "o", "   Grace over. Every 10s the coordinator looks for chunks with fewer than 3\r\n   counted replicas, and orders a node-to-node copy from a verified replica\r\n   (the coordinator never touches the bytes):\r\n"]
[49.56218, "o", "\r\u001b[K   repair copies landed: 0 of 8"]
[50.260029, "o", "\r\u001b[K   repair copies landed: 0 of 8"]
[50.998484, "o", "\r\u001b[K   repair copies landed: 0 of 8"]
[51.735628, "o", "\r\u001b[K   repair copies landed: 0 of 8"]
[52.487456, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.505126, "o", "     47.6s  chunk 0 copied to node2\r\n"]
[52.519184, "o", "     47.6s  chunk 1 copied to node3\r\n"]
[52.533611, "o", "     47.6s  chunk 2 copied to node4\r\n"]
[52.547775, "o", "     47.6s  chunk 5 copied to node3\r\n"]
[52.561338, "o", "     47.6s  chunk 6 copied to node4\r\n"]
[52.574542, "o", "     47.7s  chunk 8 copied to node2\r\n"]
[52.580724, "o", "\r\u001b[K   repair copies landed: 6 of 8"]
[53.312747, "o", "\r\n"]
[53.330805, "o", "     48.4s  chunk 4 copied to node2\r\n"]
[53.345056, "o", "     48.4s  chunk 9 copied to node3\r\n"]
[53.350527, "o", "\r\u001b[K   repair copies landed: 8 of 8"]
[53.350558, "o", "\r\n"]
[56.42715, "o", "   \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m every chunk is back to 3 healthy replicas, and each new copy verifies on disk\r\n"]
[56.60772, "o", "   chunk     node1   node2   node3   node4\r\n              DEAD   ALIVE   ALIVE   ALIVE\r\n       0         H       R       H       H\r\n       1         H       H       R       H\r\n       2         H       H       H       R\r\n       3         .       H       H       H\r\n       4         H       R       H       H\r\n       5         H       H       R       H\r\n       6         H       H       H       R\r\n"]
[56.60773, "o", "       7         .       H       H       H\r\n       8         H       R       H       H\r\n       9         H       H       R       H\r\n   H = replica from the upload, R = copied by repair, BAD = marked bad, . = none\r\n"]
[56.609371, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m── 4/6  The node comes back \u001b[0m\r\n"]
[56.60938, "o", "   Starting node1. It must send 2 heartbeats in a row before it counts as ALIVE.\r\n"]
[58.680616, "o", "      2.1s  DEAD → ALIVE\r\n"]
[58.833777, "o", "   \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node1 is ALIVE; its 8 old copies verify and count again\r\n   Those chunks now have 4 replicas. The extra copy is kept on purpose: removing\r\n"]
[58.833785, "o", "   it would be rebalancing, which this system leaves out (see DECISIONS.md).\r\n"]
[58.833818, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m── 5/6  Corrupt a replica, download anyway \u001b[0m\r\n"]
[58.975256, "o", "   Flipping one byte of chunk 3's file on node2's disk (a silent disk error).\r\n"]
[59.179439, "o", "   osctl get, reading node2's replica first:\r\n"]
[59.580703, "o", "      chunk 3: node2's copy failed its SHA-256 check → read from the next replica\r\n"]
[59.585048, "o", "      reported it; the coordinator asked node2 to verify its own copy, and marked it BAD\r\n"]
[59.657528, "o", "   \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m the download is byte-identical to the original\r\n"]
[59.744563, "o", "   \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node2's replica of chunk 3 is BAD in Postgres; reads skip it from now on\r\n   Chunk 3 is down to 2 healthy replicas; the only node without one is node1:\r\n"]
[59.855348, "o", "      0.1s  chunk 3 copied to node1\r\n"]
[60.097331, "o", "   \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m chunk 3 is back to 3 healthy replicas\r\n"]
[60.097369, "o", "   \u001b[2mnode2's BAD file stays until garbage collection deletes it, 60s later (stage 8).\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[60.097394, "o", "\r\n"]
[60.097412, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m── 6/6  Final replica state (osctl stat) \u001b[0m\r\n"]
[60.116455, "o", "   key:       demo/photo-archive.bin\r\n   object:    c44a13f4-3ad8-4227-bf90-5f9cd160c465\r\n"]
[60.116466, "o", "   size:      41943040\r\n   committed: 2026-10-30T04:23:20Z\r\n   chunks:    10\r\n"]
[60.279417, "o", "   chunk     node1   node2   node3   node4\r\n             ALIVE   ALIVE   ALIVE   ALIVE\r\n       0         H       R       H       H\r\n       1         H       H       R       H\r\n       2         H       H       H       R\r\n"]
[60.279422, "o", "       3         R     BAD       H       H\r\n       4         H       R       H       H\r\n       5         H       H       R       H\r\n       6         H       H       H       R\r\n"]
[60.279429, "o", "       7         .       H       H       H\r\n       8         H       R       H       H\r\n       9         H       H       R       H\r\n   H = replica from the upload, R = copied by repair, BAD = marked bad, . = none\r\n"]
[62.146716, "o", "   \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m every chunk has at least 3 healthy replicas, and every one of them verifies on disk\r\n"]
[62.485267, "o", "   \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m a final download (replicas in random order) is byte-identical\r\n"]
[63.399636, "o", "   \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m the flipped byte is restored; the file stays BAD in Postgres (BAD is final)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[32mPASS\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[63.630015, "x", "0"]
